  "dom_id": "step-q99937",
  "name": "Question 10",
  "problem": "$8÷\\frac{3}{7}=$",
  "worked_solution": "Dividing a whole number by a fraction is equivalent to multiplying the whole number by the reciprocal of the fraction.\n\nFirst, we write $8$ as an improper fraction:\n\n$$\n8=\\frac{8}{1}\n$$\n\nNext, we note that the reciprocal of $\\frac{3}{7}$ is $\\frac{7}{3}.$ \n\nSo, we have\n\n$$\n8÷\\frac{3}{7}=\\frac{8}{1}÷\\frac{3}{7}=\\frac{8}{1}\\times \\frac{7}{3}.\n$$\n\n \n\nNow, we multiply our fractions. \n\n$$\n\\frac{8}{1}\\times \\frac{7}{3}=\\frac{8\\times 7}{1\\times 3}=\\frac{56}{3}\n$$\n\nFinally, we write the resulting improper fraction as a mixed number:\n\n$$\n\\frac{56}{3}=18\\,\\text{R}\\,2=18\\,\\frac{2}{3}\n$$",
